{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b56-1846-73fd-b97f-e12143750a0e","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/context/phase1/spec/ShiftProof-frontend.md","limit":2000},"result":"... (truncated)\neployments.json` at build time. The shape below is illustrative; do not duplicate addresses in two sources:\\n   187\\t\\n   188\\t```ts\\n   189\\texport const DEPLOYMENTS = {\\n   190\\t  testnet: {\\n   191\\t    chainId: 5042002,\\n   192\\t    name: \\\"Arc Testnet\\\",\\n   193\\t    rpc: \\\"https://rpc.testnet.arc.io\\\",\\n   194\\t    explorer: \\\"https://explorer.testnet.arc.io\\\",\\n   195\\t    usdc: \\\"0x3600000000000000000000000000000000000000\\\",\\n   196\\t    contract: \\\"0x...\\\",       // filled after Studio deploy\\n   197\\t    deploymentBlock: 0,      // filled from the receipt\\n   198\\t  },\\n   199\\t  mainnet: {\\n   200\\t    chainId: 5042,\\n   201\\t    name: \\\"Arc Mainnet\\\",\\n   202\\t    rpc: \\\"https://rpc.mainnet.arc.io\\\",\\n   203\\t    explorer: \\\"https://explorer.arc.io\\\",\\n   204\\t    usdc: \\\"0x3600000000000000000000000000000000000000\\\",\\n   205\\t    contract: \\\"0x...\\\",       // filled after human deploy\\n   206\\t    deploymentBlock: 0,\\n   207\\t  },\\n   208\\t} as const;\\n   209\\t```\\n   210\\t\\n   211\\t- The app defaults to mainnet for the submission build; a `?network=testnet` query or a build flag selects testnet.\\n   212\\t- `deployments.json` is committed and is the single source of truth for addresses.\\n   213\\t- No runtime admin can change the contract address. A change requires a new build and a new deployment; the repo history shows it.\\n   214\\t\\n   215\\t### 13.10 Hosting options\\n   216\\t\\n   217\\t\\n   218\\t\\n   219\\t### 14.4 Fork and integration tests\\n   220\\t\\n   221\\t- `arc-forge test --network arc` against Arc Testnet runtime `[V: docs deploy-on-arc]`.\\n   222\\t- A fork test with the real testnet USDC address `0x3600…0000`; verify `decimals() == 6`, `transfer`/`transferFrom` behavior, and balances.\\n   223\\t- An integration script deploys to testnet, creates two shifts, clocks, attests, claims, refunds, cancels, and asserts the USDC balance changes.\\n   224\\t- Use small testnet amounts (1–2 USDC/hour) to stay within the Circle faucet’s 20 USDC per 2 hours `[V: S§5.1]`.\\n   225\\t\\n   226\\t### 14.5 Frontend and E2E tests\\n   227\\t\\n   228\\tManual E2E with two Rabby accounts on testnet:\\n   229\\t\\n   230\\t1. Employer creates a 4h × 1 USDC shift; worker is a different address. Approve exact 4 USDC; create.\\n   231\\t2. Worker connects, sees the shift, clocks in/out.\\n   232\\t3. Employer attests 4h; worker claims 4 USDC; balances and receipt match.\\n   233\\t4. Employer creates a 2h × 1 USDC shift; attests 1h; anyone refunds 1 USDC; worker claims 1 USDC.\\n   234\\t5. Employer creates a 1h × 1 USDC shift; cancels before clock-in; full refund.\\n   235\\t6. Wrong wallet: employer tries to claim; worker tries to attest; UI explains before signing.\\n   236\\t7. Wrong network: switch to Ethereum; app disables writes and offers Arc.\\n   237\\t8. Insufficient gas: drain the test wallet; app shows the shortfall.\\n   238\\t9. Refresh/reopen: local history and public receipt still work; no backend.\\n   239\\t10. Mobile viewport: buttons and amounts are readable; wallet connect works in the Rabby browser.\\n   240\\t\\n   241\\tIf Vitest is added, unit-test the amount formatter, status labels, and error decoder. Do not add a heavy E2E framework at the expense of the mainnet proof.\\n   242\\t\\n   243\\t### 14.6 Mainnet rehearsal\\n   244\\t\\n   245\\t- Read `eth_chainId` (5042), `USDC.decimals()` (6), and the deployer/worker balances before any signature `[V: B1, B2, N3]`.\\n   246\\t- Simulate `createShift`, `attest`, `claim`, `refundUnused`, and `cancel` with `eth_call`/`simulateContract` from the actual wallets. A simulation is not a guarantee, but it catches guards/allowance errors.\\n   247\\t- Execute the smallest possible real shift first (e.g., 1 USDC total) to validate the full path before the 20/10 USDC demo shifts. This is a real mainnet transaction and needs per-tx approval.\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01BUfRDV5neo59191iSbpSvy\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
